---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import { PageHero } from '@oimlsmart/site-shell'
import { COMPONENT_ASSET_BASE } from '../data/site-meta'
---

<Base description="OIML SMART Recommendations — the published, expert-authored executable Recommendations.">
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-14">
    <PageHero
      eyebrow="OIML SMART · Component 1"
      title="SMART Recommendations"
      lede="A Recommendation published as an executable model, authored by experts, citable to the clause — the document and the machine-readable form are one artifact."
      logo={{ name: 'smart-rec', alt: 'The SMART Recommendations logo.', base: COMPONENT_ASSET_BASE }}
    />
    <section class="mt-10 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="border border-rule rounded-lg p-6 bg-paper-raised">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-2">What a SMART Recommendation is</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">The metrological and technical requirements of a Recommendation, modeled as subjects, processes, constraints, and promises. Every element cites its clause in the source publication, so the model reads against the document line by line.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="border border-rule rounded-lg p-6 bg-paper-raised">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-2">What it replaces</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">The PDF as the only form of the Recommendation. The SMART Recommendation keeps the prose, and adds the executable form beside it: requirements evaluate, tests run, forms compute, certificates verify — by machine, not by hand.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="border border-rule rounded-lg p-6 bg-paper-raised">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-2">Who authors it</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">The OIML technical committees, in SMART Studio. The authoring guides walk from an empty package to a published edition: subjects, requirements, conformance tests, forms, packaging, validation.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="border border-rule rounded-lg p-6 bg-paper-raised">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-2">What exists today</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">R 60 (load cells) is the official pilot. R 91 (traffic speed meters), R 129 (multi-dimensional measuring instruments), and R 144 (gas analytical systems) are demo models. The OIML-CS scheme is modeled beside them.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <p class="mt-10 text-sm"><a href="/recs/docs/" class="text-accent font-medium">Read the authoring documentation →</a></p>
  </main>
</Base>
